{"id":"15.9","doc":"T","title":"Register Summary","words":1124,"blocks":[{"t":"p","s":[{"n":1,"c":[{"t":"text","v":"The addresses of registers starting from PMS in this section are relative to the Permission Control base address, and the addresses of registers starting from APB in this section are relative to the ABP Controller base address."}]},{"n":2,"c":[{"t":"text","v":"Both base address are provided in Table 4.3-3 in "},{"t":"xref","id":"4","c":[{"t":"text","v":"Chapter 4"}]},{"t":"text","v":" System and Memory."}]}]},{"t":"p","s":[{"n":3,"c":[{"t":"text","v":"Note that, all registers with CORE_X in this section apply to both CPUs."}]},{"n":4,"c":[{"t":"text","v":"The list of registers below is for CPU0 only."}]},{"n":5,"c":[{"t":"text","v":"CPU1 shares exactly the same set of registers."}]},{"n":6,"c":[{"t":"text","v":"Adding 0x0400 to the offset of the equivalent of CPU0 register gives you address for CPU1 registers."}]},{"n":7,"c":[{"t":"text","v":"For example, the offset for CPU0 register "},{"t":"reg","v":"PMS_CORE_0_IRAM0_PMS_MONITOR_0_REG"},{"t":"text","v":" is 0x00E4, the offset for CPU1 equivalent "},{"t":"reg","v":"PMS_CORE_1_IRAM0_PMS_MONITOR_0_REG"},{"t":"text","v":" should be 0x00E4 + 0x0400, which is 0x04E4."}]}]},{"t":"p","s":[{"n":8,"c":[{"t":"text","v":"The abbreviations given in Column Access are explained in Section Access Types for Registers."}]}]},{"t":"p","s":[{"n":9,"c":[{"t":"b","c":[{"t":"text","v":"Permission Control (PMS) registers: Configuration Register"}]}]}]},{"t":"table","head":[[{"t":"text","v":"Name"}],[{"t":"text","v":"Description"}],[{"t":"text","v":"Address"}],[{"t":"text","v":"Access"}]],"rows":[{"n":10,"c":[[{"t":"reg","v":"PMS_APB_PERIPHERAL_ACCESS_0_REG"}],[{"t":"text","v":"APB peripheral configuration register 0"}],[{"t":"text","v":"0x0008"}],[{"t":"text","v":"R/W"}]]},{"n":11,"c":[[{"t":"reg","v":"PMS_APB_PERIPHERAL_ACCESS_1_REG"}],[{"t":"text","v":"APB peripheral configuration register 1"}],[{"t":"text","v":"0x000C"}]